From 13fcbbc8f815731f09d3deaf9a4bed577a44c99e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pooya Parsa <pooya@pi0.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:16:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: add kw_defconfig

A hand-written list of explicit choices for unkernel (never savedefconfig
output; Kconfig drops options whose dependencies are not met without a
word, so check .config after a change). Beyond the basics (UP, no
modules, initramfs, hvc console, printk):

  devices          kwblk with ext4 (root=/dev/wda), kwnet with PACKET
                   (udhcpc), kwfb, kwinput with INPUT_EVDEV (MOUSEDEV,
                   INPUT_KEYBOARD, INPUT_MOUSE and HID_SUPPORT off),
                   kwsnd with OSS PCM emulation (no PCM timer, no
                   /proc/asound), kwvsock with VSOCKETS_DIAG (no
                   VSOCKETS_LOOPBACK), kwshm
  BINFMT_MISC      other architectures' binaries through qemu-user
  OVERLAY_FS       a writable root over the initramfs, upper layer on
                   the data disk; the optional features stay off, since
                   the lower layer is unpacked again at every boot
  EROFS_FS         a distro's read-only root image on kwblk, zstd
                   compressed (lz4 maps scattered pages with vm_map_ram,
                   which the flat vmalloc cannot do); xattrs with POSIX
                   ACLs and security.* (file capabilities)
  9P_FS, NET_9P_FD host file systems: a guest program connects AF_VSOCK
                   to the host and mounts trans=fd on it (NET_9P
                   selects NETFS_SUPPORT; no virtio transport)

systemd 255 (Ubuntu 24.04) runs as PID 1 with no failed units with
CGROUPS (cgroup2, no controllers), NAMESPACES (UTS, IPC, PID, NET), KCMP,
FANOTIFY, AUTOFS_FS and EXT4_FS_SECURITY. Cheap options that programs
probe for, about 200 KB of lowered kernel and 25 KiB of RAM together:
CGROUP_PIDS, USER_NS, CHECKPOINT_RESTORE, PSI, TASKSTATS with
TASK_XACCT and TASK_IO_ACCOUNTING, USERFAULTFD, IP_MULTICAST, UNIX_DIAG,
PACKET_DIAG, NETLINK_DIAG, BLK_DEV_LOOP (MIN_COUNT=0: 8 loop devices up
front cost 760 KiB of RAM), TUN and MAGIC_SYSRQ.
SECCOMP with SECCOMP_FILTER, for sandboxes (bubblewrap, browsers), adds
12 KB.

Off on purpose: BPF_SYSCALL and KEYS (systemd copes with ENOSYS),
RSEQ (needs arch support), IPV6, and COREDUMP (the ELF core
writer needs elf_core_copy_task_fpregs, which arch/wasm lacks, so a
fault with a core limit would be a wasm trap).

PROC_MEM_ALWAYS_FORCE rather than 7.3's PROC_MEM_FORCE_PTRACE: ptrace
has no regsets, and programs patch their own code through
/proc/self/mem. TIME_NS is listed, as its offsets apply in the syscalls.

FRAME_WARN=3072: snmp_seq_show() (net/ipv4/proc.c) has a 2304-byte
frame. On wasm, clang passes variadic arguments in a buffer on the
shadow stack and gives each call site its own 16-byte slot, which stack
colouring never merges; snmp_seq_show() unrolls into 129 seq_printf()
calls. Built with FRAME_WARN=1024, no other function warns.

Signed-off-by: Pooya Parsa <pooya@pi0.io>
---
 arch/wasm/configs/kw_defconfig | 186 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 186 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/wasm/configs/kw_defconfig

diff --git a/arch/wasm/configs/kw_defconfig b/arch/wasm/configs/kw_defconfig
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..eb90662a5f9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/wasm/configs/kw_defconfig
@@ -0,0 +1,186 @@
+# unkernel: wasm64 kernel, emulated riscv64 user mode (kwemu)
+# CONFIG_LOCALVERSION_AUTO is not set
+CONFIG_DEFAULT_HOSTNAME="unkernel"
+CONFIG_SYSVIPC=y
+CONFIG_POSIX_MQUEUE=y
+CONFIG_NO_HZ_IDLE=y
+CONFIG_HIGH_RES_TIMERS=y
+# systemd: cgroup2, namespaces, kcmp, fanotify, autofs
+CONFIG_CGROUPS=y
+CONFIG_CGROUP_PIDS=y
+CONFIG_NAMESPACES=y
+# unshare -r, bubblewrap, rootless tools, the Chromium sandbox
+CONFIG_USER_NS=y
+# /proc/PID/task/TID/children, map_files; CRIU
+CONFIG_CHECKPOINT_RESTORE=y
+# /proc/pressure (systemd-oomd), /proc/PID/io (iotop, htop)
+CONFIG_PSI=y
+CONFIG_TASKSTATS=y
+CONFIG_TASK_XACCT=y
+CONFIG_TASK_IO_ACCOUNTING=y
+# /proc/PID/mem writable without being a ptracer (ptrace has no regsets):
+# programs that patch their own code through /proc/self/mem
+CONFIG_PROC_MEM_ALWAYS_FORCE=y
+# time namespaces (unshare -T); the offsets apply in the syscalls (no vDSO)
+CONFIG_TIME_NS=y
+CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INITRD=y
+# CONFIG_RD_BZIP2 is not set
+# CONFIG_RD_LZMA is not set
+# CONFIG_RD_XZ is not set
+# CONFIG_RD_LZO is not set
+# CONFIG_RD_LZ4 is not set
+# CONFIG_RD_ZSTD is not set
+CONFIG_CC_OPTIMIZE_FOR_PERFORMANCE=y
+CONFIG_EXPERT=y
+CONFIG_KCMP=y
+CONFIG_USERFAULTFD=y
+# CONFIG_KALLSYMS is not set
+# CONFIG_IO_URING is not set
+# CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL is not set
+# CONFIG_COREDUMP is not set
+# CONFIG_SWAP is not set
+# CONFIG_COMPAT_BRK is not set
+# CONFIG_MODULES is not set
+CONFIG_SECCOMP=y
+CONFIG_SECCOMP_FILTER=y
+CONFIG_BINFMT_ELF=y
+CONFIG_BINFMT_SCRIPT=y
+CONFIG_BINFMT_MISC=y
+CONFIG_NET=y
+CONFIG_PACKET=y
+CONFIG_UNIX=y
+CONFIG_INET=y
+CONFIG_IP_MULTICAST=y
+# policy routing (ip rule, more than one table): tailscale's table 52,
+# source-based routes
+CONFIG_IP_ADVANCED_ROUTER=y
+CONFIG_IP_MULTIPLE_TABLES=y
+# ss(8) for unix, packet and netlink sockets (INET_DIAG is on by default)
+CONFIG_UNIX_DIAG=y
+CONFIG_PACKET_DIAG=y
+CONFIG_NETLINK_DIAG=y
+# AF_VSOCK to the host (kwvsock, when the host offers it); ss --vsock
+CONFIG_VSOCKETS=y
+CONFIG_VSOCKETS_DIAG=y
+# CONFIG_VSOCKETS_LOOPBACK is not set
+CONFIG_KWVSOCK=y
+# CONFIG_IPV6 is not set
+# CONFIG_WIRELESS is not set
+# CONFIG_ETHTOOL_NETLINK is not set
+CONFIG_DEVTMPFS=y
+CONFIG_DEVTMPFS_MOUNT=y
+# CONFIG_FW_LOADER is not set
+# CONFIG_ALLOW_DEV_COREDUMP is not set
+# loop devices on demand through /dev/loop-control (8 up front cost 760 KiB)
+CONFIG_BLK_DEV_LOOP=y
+CONFIG_BLK_DEV_LOOP_MIN_COUNT=0
+CONFIG_BLK_DEV_KWBLK=y
+CONFIG_NETDEVICES=y
+# a throwaway interface (ip link add type dummy)
+CONFIG_DUMMY=y
+# /dev/net/tun: openvpn, wireguard-go, tailscale
+CONFIG_TUN=y
+# a link into a network namespace (containers, ip netns)
+CONFIG_VETH=y
+# CONFIG_ETHERNET is not set
+# CONFIG_WLAN is not set
+CONFIG_KWNET=y
+# kwinput: keyboard and mouse as evdev devices when the host has a display
+CONFIG_INPUT=y
+# CONFIG_INPUT_MOUSEDEV is not set
+CONFIG_INPUT_EVDEV=y
+CONFIG_INPUT_KWINPUT=y
+# CONFIG_INPUT_KEYBOARD is not set
+# CONFIG_INPUT_MOUSE is not set
+# CONFIG_HID_SUPPORT is not set
+# CONFIG_SERIO is not set
+# CONFIG_VT is not set
+CONFIG_UNIX98_PTYS=y
+# CONFIG_LEGACY_PTYS is not set
+CONFIG_HVC_WASM=y
+# CONFIG_HW_RANDOM is not set
+# CONFIG_HWMON is not set
+# kwfb: /dev/fb0 when the host has a display, no fbcon (no VT)
+CONFIG_FB=y
+CONFIG_FB_KWFB=y
+# kwshm: the host reads and writes shmem files in place, /dev/kwshm
+CONFIG_KWSHM=y
+# /dev/udmabuf: dma-bufs from memfds (lavapipe exports its images so)
+CONFIG_UDMABUF=y
+# kwsnd: ALSA playback when the host has audio, plus OSS /dev/dsp for SDL 1.2
+CONFIG_SOUND=y
+CONFIG_SND=y
+CONFIG_SND_OSSEMUL=y
+# CONFIG_SND_MIXER_OSS is not set
+CONFIG_SND_PCM_OSS=y
+# CONFIG_SND_PCM_OSS_PLUGINS is not set
+# CONFIG_SND_PCM_TIMER is not set
+# CONFIG_SND_PROC_FS is not set
+# CONFIG_SND_CTL_FAST_LOOKUP is not set
+CONFIG_SND_KWSND=y
+# CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT is not set
+# kwvirtio: virtio devices of the host (only virtio-gpu so far), when it
+# offers them; no other virtio transport or device driver
+CONFIG_VIRTIO_MENU=y
+CONFIG_KWVIRTIO=y
+# CONFIG_VIRTIO_BALLOON is not set
+# CONFIG_VIRTIO_INPUT is not set
+# CONFIG_VIRTIO_MMIO is not set
+# /dev/dri/card0 (virtio_gpu, KMS and GEM shmem objects) when the host
+# offers virtio-gpu; no fbdev emulation (kwfb is /dev/fb0), no panic screen
+CONFIG_DRM=y
+# CONFIG_DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION is not set
+# CONFIG_DRM_PANIC is not set
+CONFIG_DRM_VIRTIO_GPU=y
+CONFIG_DRM_VIRTIO_GPU_KMS=y
+# what DRM would bring along for hardware displays: I2C (DDC), the HDMI
+# infoframe library, panels and the panel bridge, and devmem TCP (dma-buf)
+# CONFIG_DRM_DDC is not set
+# CONFIG_DRM_HDMI_INFOFRAMES is not set
+# CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_BRIDGE is not set
+# CONFIG_NET_DEVMEM is not set
+# CONFIG_VHOST_MENU is not set
+CONFIG_EXT4_FS=y
+CONFIG_EXT4_FS_POSIX_ACL=y
+CONFIG_EXT4_FS_SECURITY=y
+CONFIG_FANOTIFY=y
+CONFIG_AUTOFS_FS=y
+CONFIG_OVERLAY_FS=y
+# /dev/fuse for user space file systems (sshfs, rclone mount); built in,
+# since there are no modules
+CONFIG_FUSE_FS=y
+CONFIG_PROC_FS=y
+CONFIG_SYSFS=y
+CONFIG_TMPFS=y
+CONFIG_TMPFS_POSIX_ACL=y
+# erofs: a distro's read-only root image on kwblk, compressed with zstd;
+# xattrs with ACLs and security.* (file capabilities). lz4, which
+# EROFS_FS_ZIP always brings, fails here: it maps scattered pages with
+# vmap/vm_map_ram, which VMALLOC_FLAT cannot (ENOMEM). microLZMA is off.
+CONFIG_MISC_FILESYSTEMS=y
+CONFIG_EROFS_FS=y
+CONFIG_EROFS_FS_XATTR=y
+CONFIG_EROFS_FS_POSIX_ACL=y
+CONFIG_EROFS_FS_SECURITY=y
+CONFIG_EROFS_FS_BACKED_BY_FILE=y
+CONFIG_EROFS_FS_ZIP=y
+# CONFIG_EROFS_FS_ZIP_LZMA is not set
+CONFIG_EROFS_FS_ZIP_ZSTD=y
+# 9p over a file descriptor (trans=fd), such as an AF_VSOCK socket to a file
+# server on the host; the network file systems menu holds 9P_FS, and nothing
+# else in it is on
+CONFIG_NETWORK_FILESYSTEMS=y
+CONFIG_NET_9P=y
+CONFIG_NET_9P_FD=y
+CONFIG_9P_FS=y
+CONFIG_PRINTK_TIME=y
+# clang's wasm backend gives every variadic call its own 16-byte stack slot
+# for the argument buffer and never shares them, so a function with many
+# printf calls (snmp_seq_show: 129 after unrolling, 2304 bytes) passes the
+# 64-bit default of 2048. No other function here reaches 1024.
+CONFIG_FRAME_WARN=3072
+# /proc/sysrq-trigger, e.g. 'w' to list blocked tasks when the guest hangs
+CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ=y
+# CONFIG_SECTION_MISMATCH_WARN_ONLY is not set
+# CONFIG_RUNTIME_TESTING_MENU is not set
+# CONFIG_DEBUG_MISC is not set
-- 
2.56.0

